  "_source": "payment: French amortisation q = P·r/(1−(1+r)^−n), r = rate/1200 (rate = annual TIN %), rate 0 → P/n, computed with Python decimal (60 digits) and rounded half up; 0 when months ≤ 0 or principal ≤ 0. statementDates: worked out by hand from the rule in CreditCardTerms. summaries (ORC-78): full-payment card, limit 300000, a 120000 purchase in 24 instalments at 14 % made 13 months before today; quota 5762 and the interest/principal rows from the same French schedule in Python decimal (row interest = remaining·r rounded half up, principal = quota − interest); 12 quotas already charged = 55835 principal paid (movement \"capital\", a card payment), 64165 pending. balance is the account balance (all movements, also those not listed). revolvingBalance = used − open-cycle purchases − pending instalment principal. unresolved = plans whose purchase is not in movements: no quota, and their principal stays in revolvingBalance (the wrong figures the flag warns about). summaries (ORC-79): same card, no instalments; 50000 of September purchases, 30000 of October purchases and a +50000 credit on 2026-10-05. The September statement (closed 2026-10-01, charged 2026-11-01) is already paid, so the first charge is the October statement, due 2026-12-01. A credit with no category is neither a refund nor a known payment: it is left out of the charges like a payment (charge = 30000, not max(0, 30000 − 50000) = 0) and counted in uncategorized. Controls: the same credit with a transfer category (\"payment\") is a payment, and a +4000 credit with a non-transfer category (\"refund\") is a refund: charge = 30000 − 4000 = 26000, uncategorized = 0. uncategorized = credits with no category dated on or after the start of the first unpaid statement cycle. unpaidStatements (ORC-132): worked out by hand. firstUnpaid = the oldest statement whose payment date is today or later (a statement charged today is still unpaid); since = its cycle start (one month before), the first day whose card movements the summary needs.",
